{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-maintained audit of the configuration the Java services bind.",
    "",
    "The Java surface is small enough that an AST parser is not worth building: 15",
    "@ConfigurationProperties classes, 12 @Value sites, and two logback-spring.xml files.",
    "extract_config_keys.py folds this into the generated inventory.",
    "",
    "Keys are written in Spring's dotted property form. The App Configuration stores hold the",
    "equivalent slash form (spring.datasource.url <-> /spring/datasource/url); the provider",
    "strips the leading slash and converts remaining slashes to dots.",
    "",
    "Update this file when a @ConfigurationProperties class or @Value site changes.",
    "",
    "This is NOT a subset of app-config.yaml and must not be derived from it. The catalog",
    "records what should be provisioned per environment; this records what the code actually",
    "binds. Phase 2 compares the two, so deriving either from the other makes the comparison",
    "circular. Today 21 of these 31 keys are absent from the catalog.",
    "",
    "Possible improvement: spring-boot-configuration-processor is not currently declared in",
    "any pom. Adding it would make Maven emit META-INF/spring-configuration-metadata.json for",
    "every @ConfigurationProperties class, replacing most of this file. It would not replace",
    "all of it - the processor does not see @Value sites, nor loki.app, which logback-spring.xml",
    "reads via <springProperty> and which a class-only scan would wrongly report as dead."
  ],
